[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue with one fix queued. Its reports say otherwise. Read
by tenant, by the way each report came in, and by what the reporter actually wrote, they hold
separate problems. Each now has its own ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 closed on 5 October with the parser fix (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`). That
fix does not reach the one-day moves: they have a cause of their own and stay open as their own
ticket.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

### `parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first

Every tenant on file writes the day first. The parser reads the month first, so any date whose day
is twelve or less comes out with day and month swapped: booked for 2 July, invited for 7 February.
Only those dates have a swapped twin, and the reports only ever name days of twelve or less. This is the bug #4471 describes. It covers app, email and the booking-v2 form.

### `hint`: the booking-v3 form prints the wrong hint

Three tenants run `booking-v3`. Its date field prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under it. Their customers type
what the hint says, month first, and the form then reads the value the tenant's way, day first.
Only form reports from those tenants land here. The parser fix does not touch this: the swap
happens before the parser sees the date. The old table already marked these "not this ticket", and
they had no ticket of their own until now. The desk will not fix it: the booking-v3 form is
retired.

### `one-day-move`: dates move by one day, not by a month

These reports describe a day lost or gained, not a swap: Tuesday shown as Monday, a meeting held on
two days for clients in Lisbon and Toronto, an invite sent before the booking existed, every June
booking one day off. A day/month swap cannot produce any of them. That pattern points at time
zones: a date-only value turned into a moment and shown in another offset. The desk had noted
these reports (`desk-notes.json`) and the old table counted them under `parser` with a footnote.

## How the counts are made

- One report, one count: the export repeats some rows; `uniqueById` keeps each id once.
- `parser` and `hint` come from `causes.ts`, by tenant locale, booking form and channel, as before.
- `one-day-move` is the desk's own list in `desk-notes.json`, taken out of `parser`.
- Intake's tag (`meta.intakeTag`) is not used: it is guessed from the reporter's browser and
  disagrees with the tenant in both groups.

Code: `src/lib/kb/problems.ts` and `ProblemTable.svelte`. Nothing on this page is typed that the
data can count.

## What changes on the desk

- `parser`: fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`); #4471 closed on 5 October, and its
  ticket is closed.
- `hint`: won't fix, because the booking-v3 form is retired; its ticket is closed.
- `one-day-move`: still open. Closing #4471 did not close it; it needs its own fix.
- Merging by subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) did not make this
  ticket: its reports carry many different subjects. Splitting it needed the tenant, the form, the
  channel and the words. A new decision record should replace 0001 rather than edit it.

